            <div xml:id="d777">

                <pb facs="1250" n="1236" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751R.62114/7–644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary in Charge of the
                        Mission at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-10T20:00:00-04:00">July 10, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2161. Your 2287, July 6. Please point out to Massigli that this Government takes
                    an extremely serious view of the reports of the execution of the six German
                    prisoners of war and of the sanctioning <pb facs="1251" n="1237" xml:id="pg1237"
                    /> of the incident by the French authorities in North Africa. The American
                    Government is greatly concerned lest these reprisals lead to counter reprisals
                    by the German authorities against American and Allied prisoners of war. Please
                    report the reply which Massigli makes to your representations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
